  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Drain black beans, and rinse.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine beans, jalapenos, and chicken broth in a slow cooker. Season with garlic powder, chili powder, cumin, cayenne, pepper, and hot pepper sauce.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook on High for 4 hours. Reduce heat to Low, and continue cooking for 2 hours, or until you are ready to eat.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "If you are using dry beans, make sure to boil them first on the stovetop and then add them to the slower cooker. Dry beans do not get as tender in a slow cooker even if you soak them overnight."
    },
    {
      "text": "If you are pressed for time just use the canned black beans, toss the rest of the stuff into a slow cooker and add a can of diced tomatoes. I pureed about 1/2 the soup for a more authentic look, and served it with chopped green onion, sour cream, cheddar cheese and homemade guacamole. I found the amount of cayenne recommended and two minced jalapenos was just the right amount of spice. They really mellow out in the soup. YUM!"
    }
  ],
